From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: carry the weapon's splash flag on the explosion event

Water::explosion (client body of Explosion.cpp) sprays and plays the
splash sound when a weapon with <createsplash> lands under the water.
The port's explosion event now carries that flag in its `value` field;
the renderer, which knows the water height, decides whether the blast
was under it, exactly as Water::explosion does. One field, no logic.

---
diff --git a/src/common/actions/Explosion.cpp b/src/common/actions/Explosion.cpp
--- a/src/common/actions/Explosion.cpp
+++ b/src/common/actions/Explosion.cpp
@@ -96,6 +96,10 @@
 		effect.r = colour[0].asFloat();
 		effect.g = colour[1].asFloat();
 		effect.b = colour[2].asFloat();
+		// Whether this weapon splashes (Water::explosion's spray and its
+		// splash sound, in the client body below). The renderer decides if
+		// the blast is actually under the water, as Water::explosion does.
+		effect.value = params_->getCreateSplash() ? 1.0f : 0.0f;
 		ScorchDroidEffects::push(effect);
 	}
